+work:
+- title: Stress 2.0 — Trade Wind Down (TWD) Stress-Testing Data Pipeline
+  time: 2024.01 - present
+  company: Nomura (Shanghai) Information Technology Co., Ltd. · Risk and Control Technology
+  position: Analyst, Senior Software Development
+  content:
+  - 'Owned the Python side of the TWD pipeline: ingested data from UDW, Prism (ActivePivot-based risk data warehouse), market data and Excel inputs via MDX / REST / Dremio SQL / file export; built Data Object and Scenario domain models, post-processing and persistence; ~800 MB per run (4 scenario types × ~200 MB).'
+  - Led data-source migrations through business UAT sign-off.
+  - Implemented stress-factor calculations (incl. CS01) on the Fingal computation framework; integrated with the compute grid as a consumer, preparing inputs and collecting results.
+  - 'Led the MinIO object-storage redesign: new storage layout, file deletion and size accounting, upload-count validation, explicit overwrite semantics for duplicate files, fail-fast on empty inputs; optimised access patterns to avoid costly ListObjects calls.'
+  - Orchestrated daily-stress batch jobs on Prefect, adding missing wait-for dependencies; lead for Maestro, the event-monitoring system, owning code review, improvements and sign-off.
+  - Drove CI type validation support for SQL Server BITS / LONGNVARCHAR types.
+  - 'Proficient in AI-assisted development: Claude Code for old-vs-new data-source comparison, script and test generation, and incident analysis.'
+- title: Market Data Python ETL Framework Parsing Tool
+  time: 2023 - 2024
+  company: Nomura (Shanghai) Information Technology Co., Ltd. · Risk and Control Technology
+  position: Analyst, Senior Software Development
+  content:
+  - Aggregated multi-vendor market data and extracted the market-risk inputs each calculation model needs; optimised code paths across shared modules and custom models.
+  - Traced and fixed production parsing issues through logs and Dremio, working with other departments on root cause.
+  - Drove model execution from ETL semaphores; wrapped common interfaces in FastAPI; introduced a Status ID scheme for long-running calls and multi-process concurrency.
+  - Migrated the ETL project to AWS with YAML configuration, systemd and Jenkins-triggered provisioning; post-release checks and support.
+- title: Full Revaluation and Non-Managed CVA Calculation Process
+  time: 2023 - 2025
+  company: Nomura (Shanghai) Information Technology Co., Ltd. · Risk and Control Technology
+  position: Analyst, Senior Software Development
+  content:
+  - 'Lead for the NM CVA module: owned requirements, delivery and production releases, plus post-release production support.'
+  - Combined ActivePivot (Prism) risk data with trade and market data; persisted results to Dremio and AWS S3 for the downstream UI team.
+  - Built the Prefect pipeline that produces risk P/L and non-managed CVA under each stress scenario; per-trade calculation inside nodes, with high parallelism in pre-processing and the Monte Carlo ComputeGrid service.
+  - Designed a cache folder structure that isolates inputs per project; extracted multi-dimensional risk data with Lynx SCE.
+  - Ran Japan CVA batches and aggregated results across regions; resolved read/write conflicts without losing parallelism.
+- title: Scenario Extractor · Risk Data Endpoint (RDE)
+  time: lead
+  company: Nomura (Shanghai) Information Technology Co., Ltd. · Risk and Control Technology
+  position: Analyst, Senior Software Development
+  content:
+  - 'Lead for the Scenario Extractor: generated stress-scenario data and exposed it to front-end UI users through the Risk Data Endpoint API; worked directly with Risk Management on requirements and design and owned the production release.'
+- title: Lynx Trade-Data ETL Module
+  time: 2023.06 - 2023.12
+  company: Nomura (Shanghai) Information Technology Co., Ltd. · Risk and Control Technology
+  position: Analyst, Senior Software Development
+  content:
+  - 'Owned ETL and analysis of upstream trade data: database configuration, business-rule CRUD and REST API migration.'
+  - Delivered the Lynx 1.0 → 2.0 compatibility upgrade so upstream and downstream kept running through the version switch.
+internship:
+- title: Lane-line data closed loop and visualisation
+  time: 2021.07 - 2021.10
+  company: Nullmax (Shanghai) Technology Inc.
+  position: Data Loop and Visualisation Intern
+  content:
+  - Lane-line analysis and visualisation with Python (Django + Echarts.js) and Zeppelin; owned front and back end and the Echarts components.
+  - 'Data closed loop on Airflow: selected hard lane-line cases, scripted the analysis and presented it to engineers and users.'
+  - Cut million-row hard-case selection from 30 s to 6 s; wrote Shell / Python scripts and an Electron.js script-management tool.
+- title: Centralised face-detection model for AI standardisation
+  time: 2021.10 - 2021.12
+  company: Yitu (Shanghai) Corporation
+  position: AI Standardisation
+  content:
+  - Surveyed face-recognition approaches and selected models suited to centralised feature-map generation and detection.
